
for pushing files directly without first making Repository then follow these steps.

i will use shortcuts because everything is explained in the Practice-Repository

1. git init
2. git add .
3. git commit -m "message"
4. git remote add origin (url)
5. git push -u origin main

After writing git push -u then you don't need to write everyword of pushing again but simply write (git push).

6. git branch
7.git remote -v (lists all the remote repositories linked to your local Git project)


// branch Methods

for making branch
1. git checkout -b Branch1

saving changes in new branch
1. git push origin branchName

switching branch
1. git checkout branchName

deleting branch
2. git branch -d branchName

Mergin branch
1. either do it in Github 
2. git merge branchName

Updating existing file according to changes on Github
1. git pull origin main


// Reseting commits and adding

for just changes if save with git add .
1. git reset

for changes which is commited then reseting them:
1. git reset HEAD~1  (HEAD  is the default name of the latest commit)
Hent: git log will give you all of your commits 

for reseting you commits from a specific commit do:
1. git reset Hashcode ("like this 866b06a0e9e6c717b491f217ca07f60a0e5ca688")
so whatever comes after Hashcode that will be reseted

after reseting if you want the code also removed from vs code then:
1. get reset --hard Hashcode